Subject: [PATCH] icecc.bbclass: bail silently instead of fatal on NULL HOST_PREFIX

Some recipes (e.g. target-sdk-provides-dummy) override PACKAGE_ARCH so
icecc_is_allarch returns False even though the recipe inherits allarch
and has no real toolchain. Their HOST_PREFIX is empty, which triggers
bb.fatal during vardep walk of set_icecc_env and aborts parsing.

Returning "" here lets the shell wrapper's
    bbwarn "Cannot use icecc: could not get ICECC_VERSION"
path handle it gracefully.

diff --git a/meta/classes/icecc.bbclass b/meta/classes/icecc.bbclass
--- a/meta/classes/icecc.bbclass
+++ b/meta/classes/icecc.bbclass
@@ -212,7 +212,10 @@ def icecc_version(bb, d):
     if icecc_is_native(bb, d):
         archive_name = "local-host-env"
     elif d.expand('${HOST_PREFIX}') == "":
-        bb.fatal(d.expand("${PN}"), " NULL prefix")
+        # Recipes that override PACKAGE_ARCH (e.g. target-sdk-provides-dummy)
+        # leak past icecc_is_allarch but still have an empty HOST_PREFIX.
+        # Bail silently instead of fatal-ing parsing.
+        return ""
     else:
         prefix = d.expand('${HOST_PREFIX}' )
         distro = d.expand('${DISTRO}')
